# Tech Stack - feature/database (Maddi Soumya)

Database Engine : PostgreSQL (local server install; not a cloud service)
Driver / Access : node-postgres (`pg` npm package) - pure JavaScript
                  wire-protocol client, no native/compiled dependency
Schema          : Plain SQL DDL file (database/schema.sql) using native
                  Postgres ENUM types, TIMESTAMPTZ/DATE, and NUMERIC for
                  exact-precision money math. Applied via a Node
                  migration runner (database/migrate.js), which also
                  creates the target database if it does not exist yet.
Seed Data       : Programmatic seed script (database/seed.js) generating
                  real relational demo records (not static JSON)
Tooling scripts : database/reset.js (migrate + seed in one step),
                  database/verify.js (row-count + business-rule sanity
                  checks)
Config          : .env (git-ignored, per-developer) + config.js, using
                  standard PGHOST/PGPORT/PGUSER/PGPASSWORD/PGDATABASE
                  environment variables

Why this stack:
- Full relational database engine with native enum types, exact-numeric
  money columns, and constraints/triggers enforced by the server itself.
- Still fully local - runs on a PostgreSQL server installed on your own
  machine, no cloud database account required.
- No native build tooling needed to install the driver (pg is pure JS),
  unlike better-sqlite3 which failed to build on this machine due to a
  missing Visual Studio toolchain.
- A real, dynamic, queryable relational database (not static JSON),
  satisfying the "use real-time/dynamic data sources" requirement.
- Portable schema.sql / seed.js that feature/backend (Avanti) can point
  any Node-based API layer at directly (reusing the same env vars), and
  feature/frontend (Vyshnavi) can inspect with any Postgres client
  (pgAdmin, DBeaver, psql) while the API is being built.

Where things live:
  PeoplePay360_Team301/database/
    schema.sql   - full DDL: employees, departments, job positions,
                   working schedules, contracts (period-aware, with
                   overlap-prevention trigger), attendance, time off
                   types/allocations/requests, salary structures/rules,
                   payruns/payslips/payslip lines, payroll warnings,
                   roles/users (RBAC)
    migrate.js   - creates the database (if missing) and applies schema.sql
    seed.js      - inserts demo data reproducing the README's worked
                   examples (contract resolution, leave balance flow)
    reset.js     - one-shot: migrate + seed
    verify.js    - prints row counts and checks key business rules
    config.js    - loads .env and centralizes PG connection config
    .env.example - template for local Postgres connection credentials
    README.md    - setup + usage instructions for the rest of the team

Prerequisite (not committed to the repo): a running local PostgreSQL
server. Install from https://www.postgresql.org/download/ - any
version 13+ works. See database/README.md for full setup steps.
